ference on Machine Learning, pages 1188-1196."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b0-3-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hector J Levesque, Ernest Davis, and Leora Morgen-stern. 2011. The winograd schema challenge. In Aaai spring symposium: Logical formalizations of commonsense reasoning, volume 46, page 47."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b0-4-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Lajanugen Logeswaran and Honglak Lee. 2018. An efficient framework for learning sentence represen-tations. In International Conference on Learning Representations."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b0-5-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bryan McCann, James Bradbury, Caiming Xiong, and Richard Socher. 2017. Learned in translation: Con-textualized word vectors. In NIPS."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b0-6-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Oren Melamud, Jacob Goldberger, and Ido Dagan. 2016. context2vec: Learning generic context em-bedding with bidirectional LSTM. In CoNLL."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b0-7-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tomas Mikolov, Ilya Sutskever, Kai Chen, Greg S Cor-rado, and Jeff Dean. 2013. Distributed representa-tions of words and phrases and their compositional-ity. In Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 26, pages 3111-3119. Curran Associates, Inc."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b2-0-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Andriy Mnih and Geoffrey E Hinton. 2009. A scal-able hierarchical distributed language model. In D. Koller, D. Schuurmans, Y. Bengio, and L. Bot-tou, editors, Advances in Neural Information Pro-cessing Systems 21, pages 1081-1088. Curran As-sociates, Inc."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b2-1-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ankur P Parikh, Oscar Tackstr ¨¨ Dipanjan Das, and Jakob Uszkoreit. 2016. A decomposable attention model for natural language inference. In EMNLP."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b2-2-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Jeffrey Pennington, Richard Socher, and Christo-pher D. Manning. 2014. Glove: Global vectors for word representation. In Empirical Methods in Nat-ural Language Processing (EMNLP), pages 1532- 1543."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b2-3-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Matthew Peters, Waleed Ammar, Chandra Bhagavat-ula, and Russell Power. 2017. Semi-supervised se-quence tagging with bidirectional language models. In ACL."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b2-4-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Matthew Peters, Mark Neumann, Mohit Iyyer, Matt"}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b3-0-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Gardner, Christopher Clark, Kenton Lee, and Luke Zettlemoyer. 2018a. Deep contextualized word rep-resentations. In NAACL."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b5-0-ii","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[]},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Matthew Peters, Mark Neumann, Luke Zettlemoyer, and Wen-tau Yih. 2018b. Dissecting contextual word embeddings: Architecture and representation. In Proceedings of the 2018 Conference on Empiri-cal Methods in Natural Language Processing, pages 1499-1509."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p11-b5-1-